15 0 obj
<< /A 35 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating the progression from adolescent drivers like puberty, increased adiposity, and psychological stress to insulin resistance and inflammatory activation, leading to endothelial injury and culminating in early vascular phenotype alterations such as reduced FMD and increased arterial stiffness, with a feedback loop indicating impaired capillary recruitment may worsen insulin resistance.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 25 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 36 0 R /Alt (Flowchart illustrating a tiered approach to clinical data, beginning with routine measures like HbA1c, BMI, and blood pressure, progressing through practical inflammatory markers, research vascular phenotyping, and culminating in risk-informed prevention. A parallel box highlights the need for exploratory and validation research involving miRNAs, metabolomics, proteomics, ceramides, BCAAs, and AGE measurement, emphasizing the necessity to test predictive value in pediatric populations. Color-coded boxes indicate increasing research complexity and decreasing clinical feasibility from top to bottom.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
